From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antigravity <antigravity@google.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: transcode BC1-BC3 and BC7 textures directly to ASTC 4x4

Directly transcode DirectX BC1, BC2, BC3, and BC7 compressed textures into
VK_FORMAT_ASTC_4x4_UNORM_BLOCK and VK_FORMAT_ASTC_4x4_SRGB_BLOCK on Mali
hardware instead of uncompressed RGBA8.

- Reduces texture VRAM footprint by 75% (16 bytes/block instead of 64 bytes/block)
- Reduces texture memory bandwidth by 75% for sampling
- Leverages native Mali ASTC silicon texture samplers for filtering and sampling
- Adds compute shaders panvk_bc_s3tc_astc and panvk_bc_bc7_astc
- Controlled via PANVK_BC_MODE (defaults to astc, rgba8 fallback)

Purpose: 75% VRAM and bandwidth reduction for BC textures on Mali-G615
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, Dimensity 7050)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21

